  "title": "SaMer: Object-Aware Token Merging for Efficient Vision-Language Retrieval",
  "summary": "SaMer introduces a framework to preserve query-selectable object evidence in vision-language retrieval, reducing token costs while improving performance on benchmarks like Flickr30K and MSCOCO. It uses object annotations only during training and adapts only the shared projection layer with frozen vision and language backbones.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "SaMer compresses image-side post-projector tokens into $K=64$ centroids while preserving the original late-interaction interface.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SaMer reduces ColPali storage by $16.09\times$ and improves R@1 on Flickr30K and MSCOCO.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "SaMer outperforms compression baselines and shows stronger phrase-level grounding.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
